    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Issue:**\nWhen running `node <repo>/packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was not being passed through to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI, so the workflow file wasn't created.\n\n**The Fix:**\nIn `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-756), I changed how arguments are passed to the spawnSync call. Instead of relying on commander.js's variadic arguments parameter (which wasn't capturing flags correctly), I now reconstruct all arguments from `process.argv`:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst allArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : [];\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...allArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\n**Testing:**\nI rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested the command. When running `frai gate init --ci`, it now correctly creates both the `FRAI-SPEC.md` file and the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` workflow file, with the proper GitHub Actions configuration.\n\nThe changes are ready to be committed and the fix is working as expected.",
